Build a polished, highly interactive mobile prototype called:

سُهيل / Suhail

سُهيل is a smart university indoor navigation platform that helps students and visitors find classrooms, lecture halls, faculty offices, university services, and events inside university buildings.

This prototype is being created for a hackathon judging video, so it must feel like a credible, working smart-campus product — not a collection of static mockups.

==================================================
DEVICE & RESPONSIVE LAYOUT — VERY IMPORTANT
==================================================

Design the entire prototype specifically for:

iPhone 17 Pro Max

Base logical frame size:
440 × 956 pt

The prototype must fit naturally inside this viewport.

Respect:
- iOS safe areas
- Dynamic Island spacing
- rounded screen corners
- bottom home indicator area
- comfortable thumb-friendly touch targets

Do not allow:
- bottom navigation to be clipped
- floating buttons to overlap the home indicator
- search bars to collide with the Dynamic Island
- cards or bottom sheets to overflow outside the viewport
- text or buttons to be cut off

Use responsive layout behavior so the interface can adapt to similar iPhone screen sizes later, but optimize the main experience for 440 × 956 pt.

The indoor map must remain the dominant visual area.

Avoid oversized headers, oversized cards, or excessive empty spacing that reduces usable map space.

==================================================
PRODUCT PURPOSE
==================================================

The problem:

Students and visitors often struggle to locate classrooms, faculty offices, services, and events inside large university buildings.

Outdoor maps usually help users reach the building, but they do not solve the problem of navigating inside the building.

سُهيل solves this by connecting:

Indoor Navigation
University Data
AI Assistance
Student Schedule
Faculty Appointment Booking
Gamification

into one connected university experience.

==================================================
DESIGN DIRECTION
==================================================

Create a premium mobile experience inspired by the quality and interaction style of modern campus navigation applications such as Concept3D, combined with the clarity and simplicity of premium map applications.

The final design must have its own identity.

Visual style:

- Modern
- Premium
- Professional
- Minimal
- Student-friendly
- Clean white and warm neutral surfaces
- Deep green / teal primary accent
- Subtle shadows
- Rounded cards
- Refined typography
- Smooth micro-interactions
- Strong visual hierarchy

Brand name:

سُهيل
Suhail

Always write the Arabic brand exactly as:

سُهيل

Tagline:

“Your smart guide across campus.”

Do not make the interface childish.
Do not make it look like a generic dashboard.
Do not overload the interface with cards.

==================================================
THE MAP IS THE HERO
==================================================

The Map is the primary experience of سُهيل.

The Map screen is also the Home screen.

The map should occupy most of the available iPhone 17 Pro Max viewport.

This is an INDOOR university navigation application.

Do NOT create:

- car navigation
- city roads
- residential neighborhoods
- houses
- apartment layouts
- driving directions

The environment must immediately feel like a real university.

Create a realistic placeholder university building for this first version.

Include:

- Classrooms
- Lecture halls
- Computer labs
- Faculty offices
- Library areas
- Study areas
- Main lobby
- Student areas
- Restrooms
- Stairs
- Elevators
- Entrances
- Large event / innovation hall

Indoor maps should clearly show:

- corridors
- walls
- room shapes
- doors
- stairs
- elevators
- open student areas
- room labels
- navigation paths

The map should feel like a real digital campus map, not an architectural blueprint.

IMPORTANT:

For this first generation, use a realistic placeholder university layout.

A real university floor plan will be provided later.

Do not build the rest of the application in a way that depends on the placeholder map.

==================================================
BOTTOM NAVIGATION
==================================================

Use ONLY four bottom navigation tabs:

Map
Schedule
Game
Profile

Do NOT add AI as a bottom navigation tab.

The bottom navigation must:

- remain fixed
- respect the iPhone bottom safe area
- be easy to reach with one hand
- remain visible without covering important map content

==================================================
ASK SUHAIL AI
==================================================

AI must appear as a floating action button above the map.

Label:

Ask Suhail

Use a distinctive but elegant AI icon.

Place it above the bottom navigation without overlapping navigation controls.

AI should feel like an intelligent layer connected to the campus map — not a separate application.

==================================================
1. SPLASH SCREEN
==================================================

Create a premium splash / welcome screen.

Show:

سُهيل
Suhail

Tagline:

“Your smart guide across campus.”

Use a subtle modern Saudi university atmosphere.

Possible visual elements:

- modern academic architecture
- university courtyard
- greenery
- palm trees

Primary button:

Let’s Get Started

Keep this screen elegant and minimal.

==================================================
2. MAP / HOME
==================================================

After entering the application, open directly to Map.

The map should occupy most of the screen.

At the top, below the safe area, place a search field:

“Where do you want to go?”

or

“Search classrooms, offices, labs, services…”

Include:

- Current location indicator
- Room labels
- Building / area labels
- Floor selector
- Stairs / elevator indicators
- Map controls
- Ask Suhail floating button
- Bottom navigation

Possible university locations:

Building A
Building B
Building C
Library
Student Center
Innovation Hall

Keep UI elements floating above the map.

Do not replace the map with a homepage containing large cards.

==================================================
3. SEARCH EXPERIENCE
==================================================

The student taps the search field and searches:

B203

Show realistic search results.

Primary result:

B203
Classroom
Building B
Floor 2
4-minute walk

Add a realistic classroom thumbnail.

Primary action:

Start Navigation

Nearby results may include:

B201
B204
B205

Use a compact bottom sheet or floating card so the map remains visible.

The search should feel functional.

==================================================
4. INDOOR NAVIGATION
==================================================

After pressing Start Navigation, enter indoor navigation mode.

Show:

- Indoor floor map
- Current user position
- Destination pin
- Highlighted walking route
- Remaining distance
- Walking time
- Current floor
- Navigation instruction banner

Example instructions:

“Continue straight – 25 m”

“Turn right”

“Take the stairs to Floor 2”

“B203 is on your right”

The current-location indicator should visibly move between navigation states.

Animate route progress.

The map may subtly pan or reposition as the user progresses so it feels like a real navigation application.

Keep the movement smooth and easy to follow in a screen recording.

==================================================
5. FLOOR TRANSITION
==================================================

Support navigation between university floors.

Example:

Current:
Floor 1

Instruction:

“Take the stairs to Floor 2”

Show clear:

Stairs
Elevator

Then transition visually to:

Floor 2

The transition should feel like the same university building rather than loading an unrelated map.

==================================================
6. ARRIVAL + CHECK-IN
==================================================

When the student reaches B203, show an engaging but professional arrival state.

Display:

✓ You made it!

“You arrived at B203 before class starts.”

Example:

Arrival:
9:54 AM

Class starts:
10:00 AM

Reward:

+50 Points

Include a subtle success animation.

Do not make the celebration childish.

Button:

View in Game

==================================================
7. GAME
==================================================

Create a clean gamification screen.

Purpose:

Encourage punctuality, engagement, and campus exploration.

Example:

Level 4
Explorer

650 / 1000 points

Achievements:

Early Bird
Arrived on time for 3 classes

Campus Explorer
Visited 5 university locations

3-Day Streak
Arrived on time for 3 consecutive days

Show:

- Current points
- Level
- Progress
- Streak
- Achievements

The +50 points earned after arriving at B203 should be visually reflected here.

Gamification is supportive.

This should NOT look like a children's game.

==================================================
8. SUHAIL AI EXPERIENCE
==================================================

Return to Map.

When the user presses:

Ask Suhail

open an elegant bottom sheet / chat overlay.

Keep some of the campus map visible in the background.

Header:

Suhail AI

Subtitle:

Your campus assistant

The student asks:

“Where is the hall for today’s FARQ Hackathon?”

IMPORTANT:

Always write:

FARQ Hackathon

Never write:

Fariq
Firaq
Faraq

Suhail responds:

“The FARQ Hackathon is being held today at Innovation Hall, Building C, Ground Floor.”

Also show:

“It starts at 1:00 PM and is approximately a 4-minute walk from your current location.”

Display a location card:

Innovation Hall
Building C
Ground Floor

Actions:

Navigate There
Show on Map

The response should feel based on campus data rather than a generic chatbot answer.

==================================================
9. FARQ HACKATHON NAVIGATION
==================================================

When the user presses:

Navigate There

close the AI panel automatically.

Return to the Map.

Start navigation from the current user position to:

Innovation Hall
Building C
Ground Floor

Display the navigation route clearly.

