==================================================
DATA-DRIVEN STRUCTURE
==================================================

Make the prototype feel like it could receive real university data.

Use realistic mock structured data.

Conceptually organize data as:

Building
→ Floor
→ Room
→ Room Type
→ Map Position

Faculty
→ Department
→ Office
→ Availability

Event
→ Event Name
→ Date
→ Time
→ Venue
→ Building
→ Floor

Class
→ Course
→ Time
→ Classroom

Student
→ Schedule
→ Appointments
→ Points
→ Achievements

The UI should feel driven by this information rather than being a set of unrelated hard-coded screens.

Real university data will replace this mock data later.

==================================================
EXACT DEMO FLOW
==================================================

The clickable prototype must support this exact story:

Splash
→ Map

Student searches:
B203

→ B203 result
→ Start Navigation
→ Indoor Navigation
→ Floor Transition
→ Arrive at B203
→ Check-in
→ +50 Points
→ View Game

Then:

Return to Map
→ Ask Suhail

Student asks:

“Where is the hall for today’s FARQ Hackathon?”

→ Suhail identifies Innovation Hall
→ Navigate There
→ Indoor navigation
→ Arrive at Innovation Hall

Then:

Open Schedule
→ View classes
→ View FARQ Hackathon
→ Book Appointment
→ Choose Dr. Ahmad Alqahtani
→ Select 11:30 AM
→ Confirm Appointment

This journey should be smooth enough to record as approximately a 2-minute hackathon demonstration.

==================================================
INTERACTION QUALITY
==================================================

Interaction quality is extremely important.

Include:

- Tappable controls
- Smooth page transitions
- Interactive search
- Moving user-location indicator
- Animated navigation route
- Map panning
- Floor transitions
- Bottom sheets
- AI overlay
- Selected-state feedback
- Subtle loading states
- Arrival celebration
- Animated point increase
- Appointment time selection
- Fixed bottom navigation

The prototype must NOT feel like static screenshots.

==================================================
MAP VIEWPORT PRIORITY
==================================================

Because this prototype targets iPhone 17 Pro Max 440 × 956 pt:

Maintain generous map visibility.

Do not allow UI overlays to permanently consume most of the screen.

When a bottom sheet opens:

- use compact collapsed state when possible
- allow the map to remain visible
- avoid covering the entire screen unnecessarily

The user should always feel spatially connected to the campus.

==================================================
DO NOT
==================================================

Do NOT:

- create car navigation
- create road navigation
- create a city map
- make campus buildings look residential
- make indoor layouts look like houses
- add AI to bottom navigation
- add more than four bottom navigation tabs
- make Game childish
- make Innovation Hall a small room
- overload screens with text
- use desktop-style dashboard layouts
- make the home screen a collection of large cards
- ignore iPhone safe areas
- clip interface elements
- create layouts wider than the mobile viewport

==================================================
FINAL EXPERIENCE
==================================================

The final prototype should communicate:

سُهيل is a realistic smart-campus platform combining:

Indoor Navigation
+
University Data
+
AI Assistance
+
Student Schedule
+
Faculty Appointment Booking
+
Gamification

into one connected university experience.

Make it visually impressive enough for hackathon judges while remaining believable as a product that could actually be implemented by a university.

For this first generation:

Focus on the complete application structure, user experience, visual system, responsiveness, interactions, and demo flow.

Do NOT attempt to recreate a specific real university floor plan yet.

A real university floor plan will be provided later and should replace ONLY the map layout without requiring the application UI to be redesigned.